# WS-071 — response headers for wrongstack.com.
#
# READ THIS FIRST: this file does NOTHING on GitHub Pages, which is where the
# site is served from today (see CNAME). GitHub Pages cannot emit custom
# response headers at all. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages both read `_headers`
# from the publish root, so the day the site moves behind either — or behind
# Cloudflare in front of Pages, with a Transform Rule built from this list —
# the protection turns on with no further work.
#
# It is committed now because the one control that genuinely cannot be shipped
# any other way is `frame-ancestors`: a policy delivered by `<meta>` ignores
# that directive, so the meta CSP the build injects (csp.mjs) closes the script
# and exfiltration surface but leaves the site framable by any origin. The
# realistic abuse is UI redress — framing the real site under a fake
# "Download / Install" overlay to lend a malicious install command credibility.
#
# Keep the CSP below in sync with `websiteCsp()` in `csp.mjs`. The script
# hashes deliberately do not appear here: header CSP and meta CSP are
# intersected by the browser, so the meta policy's hashes still apply, and
# duplicating them would create a second place to drift.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
